<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Demetrius II Nicator</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Demetrius II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Demetrius II Nicator was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> in the second century BCE. His reign was disrupted by dynastic rivals and by a war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthians</a>, who captured him and held him prisoner for years. His captivity and the loss of eastern territory illustrate the decline of Seleucid power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/demetrius-ii-nicator.jpg" alt="Demetrius II Nicator" width="320" height="333" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Demetrius_II_Nicator_(cropped),_Ptolemais_in_Phoenicia_mint.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
